The Agency reserves the right to perform work under this Contract at any time. If the Contractor fails to timely or otherwise adequately perform any service under this Contract, the Agency may, in its absolute discretion, engage outside contractors to perform Contract work. The City reserves all of its Contract remedies and all other remedies available to it by law. Article 11

CONTRACTOR'S EMERGENCY TELEPHONE

The Contractor shall furnish the telephone numbers and pagers of at least three (3) responsible firm members or employees who can be reached 24 hours a day in times of emergencies resulting out of or in connection with the work to be performed under this Contract. Article 12

OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY REGULATIONS

The Contractor shall comply with all applicable federal, State and City Occupational Safety Standards and Regulations. Article 13

ADJUSTING THE AMOUNT OF WORK

The amount of work listed is only an estimate. The City shall have no obligation to order any particular amount of work. The City shall have the right to increase, decrease or delete in its entirety the amount of work listed. Article 14

INVOICES AND REPORTS

Payment shall be made to the Contractor within thirty (30) days after the invoice received or acceptance date in accordance with the Prompt Payment provisions of the Procurement Policy Board Rules, section 4-06. The Contractor must submit electronic Invoices (on a Monthly Basis, Per Work Order, upon project completion) via the PassPort System only. Do not email or mail invoices. In addition, please attach any required supporting documentation detailing the times and locations of all work performed, any materials installed in performance of this Agreement, and its purpose and location where installed, including the date materials were installed. If the Agreement allows for parts and materials reimbursements, please also attach supplier receipts. If Prevailing Wages apply, upload Agency’s approved time sheets and certified payroll reports. The Contractor shall submit with its invoices clear and legible copies of all suppliers’ invoices including Subcontractors' invoices for work performed. Failure to comply with any of the requirements set forth in this Agreement may result in the delay or denial of payment. All invoices submitted for payment must have the following:
1. Invoice number and date;
2. Description of services rendered (with supporting documents when applicable);
3. Applicable quantities and unit prices (extensions);
4. Service period (date from/date to);
5. Billing rates for labor or services (e.g., per/hour, per/week) (extensions);
6. Total amount due;
